{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310795,"nonce":"cibvl9rsPq8uGov3n/1qBCJ4iE4=","title":"Per-kernel wall-time breakdown for Llama 3.2 1B Q4_K_M decode after the 2026-06-07 optimization stack (flash_attn_decode, Q4_K_M paired ...","message":"Decode rate on canonical 6-token Paris (\"What is the capital of France?\")\nsits at ~30 tok/s on M1 Pro (Cranelift backend with LLVM auto-upgrade\ngated by the manifest; LLVM tier wins on long generations once JIT\ncompile amortises). Up from the 1.74 tok/s pre-flash_attn baseline.\n\n\nMeasured via `RAYZOR_KERNEL_TIMING=1` + the new `runtime/src/kernel_timing.rs`\nmodule (commit `92010bd`). Lightweight `Instant::now()` pair per FFI\nentry, RAII-guarded, atomic accumulator, atexit dump.\n\n| Kernel | Wall | % | Calls | µs/call |\n|--------|------|---|-------|---------|\n| `matmul_qt_t_f32_threaded` | 1983 ms | **84.5%** | 7233 | 274 |\n| `topk_scan` | 231 ms | 9.8% | 81 | 2848 |\n| `matmul_qkv_qt_t_f32_threaded` | 84 ms | 3.6% | 1296 | 65 |\n| `flash_attn_decode` | 51 ms | 2.2% | 1280 | 40 |\n\n80 tokens / 2.348 s timed = 34 tok/s (kernel time only; total wall 32.85\ntok/s). Distribution: 7233 / 80 ≈ 90 quantised-matmul calls per token,\nbroken into ~89 / 16 layers ≈ 5.5 per layer (FFN gate / up / down +\nattention output proj — SwiGLU fusion was tried and washed out, so\ngate / up stay separate).\n\n\n`matmul_qt_t_f32_threaded` is **84.5% of decode wall**. Any % gain on\nthis kernel propagates ~85% of that % to total tok/s.\n\nAlready-explored levers on this kernel (per memory):\n- Q4_K_M SDOT base: working +3-7% (acb80e5, a241cc9)\n- Q4_K_M 2-block paired SDOT: +3.04% Voronoi N=300 (acb80e5)\n- Q4_K_M 4-way partial-acc unroll: +1.42% short / +6.95% long (a241cc9)\n- F32 -\u003e Q4_K_M re-quant lm_head: landed (visible in load output)\n- Q6_K 2-block SDOT: -4.7% (washed out, bugs_q6k_sdot_no_win)\n- Q6_K 8-way partial unroll: washed out (bugs_q6k_partial_unroll_no_win)\n- SwiGLU gate+up fusion: -0.2% (washed out, bugs_swiglu_fusion_no_win)\n\nUnexplored levers worth microbenching BEFORE writing the full mirror:\n- Q4_K_M 3-block or 4-block paired SDOT (extension of acb80e5)\n- Software prefetch ahead in inner loop (PLDL1KEEP for next 2-block)\n- 2x2 output tile (process 2 output rows + 2 x_chunks per inner iter)\n- Per-thread x_chunk reuse across consecutive output rows\n- Lock-free per-row work distribution (currently parallel_rows fork-join)\n\n`topk_scan` at 9.8%: SIMD horizontal reduction in the 128k-vocab scan\ncould yield further gains. Already FFI-batched (90252ae); inside is a\nscalar argmax + repetition-penalty loop.\n\n\n`tools/profile_run.sh` (SIGPROF-based) is broken for CPU attribution\non this codebase: it shares the GRAPH_SITES hashmap between alloc-graph\nand CPU samples, but `tools/resolve_alloc_graph.py` treats all rows as\nalloc samples. Top \"hot\" rows are LLVM static data tables (atos\nmisattribution to nearby symbols), not real hot spots. The\n`kernel_timing` module is the reliable alternative until the\npost-processor is fixed.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_kernel_breakdown_2026_06_07` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}